course: dictionary
lesson: 5935
title: Mascots and lucky friends
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A mascot is a person, animal or object that a team, school or club keeps for good luck. It can also be a character in a big costume that stands for a team or event. Look for clues around the word: «Ferris the crab is the unofficial mascot of Rust» tells you Ferris is a friendly figure that stands for the Rust language.
explain: The word «unofficial» is a clue too. It means Ferris was not officially chosen, but people still treat it as the mascot. Check your meaning by swapping in a simple word: «Ferris is the unofficial lucky symbol of Rust» still makes sense, so mascot means a lucky symbol or friendly figure.
fact: A mascot is someone or something a group keeps for luck, or to stand for the group.
fact: «Dalmatians really were fire dogs that ran beside horse-drawn fire carts», and some American fire stations still keep one as a mascot.
fact: A school mascot might be a dancing character in a costume, while a class mascot is often a soft toy that goes home with a different child each weekend.
fact: «Rustaceans» is a joke on crustaceans, like crabs. Rust is a coding language, not a language about crabs.
exercise: «Ferris the crab is the unofficial mascot of Rust.» What is a mascot here? | *A friendly figure that stands for a group | A rule every coder must follow | A crab that lives in the sea | A kind of coding mistake
exercise: A soft toy goes home with a different child each weekend in Mrs Green's class. What is the toy called? | A team captain | A lucky football | *A class mascot | A school bell
exercise: Mia keeps a tiny dragon figure in her pencil case for luck. Is it a mascot? | No, mascots can only be people | *Yes, a small figure kept for luck | No, it is just a decoration with no meaning | No, a mascot must be in a costume
test: Jamal says a mascot must be a real animal. Is he right? | Yes, but only at the Olympics | *No, a mascot can be a person, an animal or an object | Yes, mascots are always real animals | No, mascots never bring luck
test: Why do Rust programmers call themselves «Rustaceans»? | It is because Rust is a language about crabs | *It is a joke on crustaceans, like crabs | It is because they all love the sea
exam: In «Ferris is the unofficial mascot of Rust», what does unofficial show? | *Ferris was not officially chosen, though people treat it as the mascot | Ferris is the best mascot ever | Ferris is a real crab in the sea | Ferris only works on Tuesdays
